+
+**Goal:** Make `/discord:launch start` create a git worktree when the target is a git repo, so multiple isolated Claude sessions can run against the same repository.
+
+**Architecture:** Skill-only change to `skills/launch/SKILL.md`. `start` gains a git-detection branch: git repos launch in a fresh worktree under `/workspaces/.worktrees/`, non-git directories keep launching in place. The worktree path is an ordinary cwd, so sid derivation, tmux naming, and the daemon are untouched. No TypeScript, no `bindings.json` schema change.
