+# discord_ask confirmation refactor — design
+
+Date: 2026-05-21
+Topic: route confirmations in `/discord:launch` through `discord_ask` when
+triggered from Discord, and replace the brittle `sleep 3 + zellij action
+write 13` dev-channels Enter with a polled delivery that runs against a
+transient pty-backed client.
+
+## Problem
+
+The `/discord:launch` skill has three confirmation sites whose current
+implementation is either invisible to the Discord user or empirically
+fragile:
+
+1. **Step 8 (dev-channels Enter)** — after `claude
+   --dangerously-load-development-channels` is started in the spawned pane,
+   the skill does `sleep 3 && zellij -s <session> action write 13` to dismiss
+   the "I am using this for local development" prompt. Two failure modes
+   were observed in empirical tests:
+   - `zellij action` is a silent no-op when no client is attached to the
+     target session (returns exit 0, drops the action). The launch flow
+     creates the session via `zellij attach --create-background` and runs
+     Claude inside it via `zellij run --in-place --close-replaced-pane`;
+     neither attaches a client, so today's `sleep 3 && action write 13` is
+     in fact a no-op against the live session — this is the root cause of
+     the reported "无法发送确定" symptom.
+   - The 3 s wait is a heuristic; even with a client attached, on a slow
+     host the prompt is not yet rendered when the Enter is sent.
+
+   (The Zellij startup-tip overlay, which is a separate failure mode in a
+   naive `zellij attach -c` flow, does **not** apply here: `run --in-place
+   --close-replaced-pane` replaces the default pane — and with it the tip
+   overlay — before any key would be delivered. The empirical test
+   `attach --create-background` + `run --in-place` confirms the active
+   pane is the Claude pane, no tip.)
+2. **Step 3 (binding conflict)** — when a repo already has a legacy in-place
+   binding and the user invokes `start`, the skill prompts the user to pick
+   "reuse" vs "new worktree". SKILL.md documents using `discord_ask` when
+   the invocation is Discord-driven, but the behavior depends on the agent
+   following that instruction; there is no integration test covering it.
+3. **`stop`** — kills the zellij session immediately with no confirmation.
+   A forged or careless Discord message can stop a running session
+   one-shot. `purge` is already terminal-only; `stop` is not.
+
+Discord users cannot see terminal AskUserQuestion prompts or click an
+in-pane Enter, so any confirmation that does not flow through Discord is
+effectively unanswerable from their side.
+
+## Solution overview
+
+Two parallel changes inside the launch skill:
+
+1. **Discord-triggered confirmations go through `discord_ask`.** When the
+   invocation context contains a `<channel source="discord" ...>`
+   notification — i.e. the request came from Discord, not the terminal —
+   the skill asks the user via `discord_ask` and only proceeds on an
+   affirmative click. Terminal-triggered invocations are unchanged.
+2. **The dev-channels Enter delivery becomes robust.** The brittle
+   `sleep 3 + action write 13` is replaced with a small shell helper that
+   (a) briefly attaches a pty-backed background client via `script` so
+   `zellij action` actually delivers, (b) polls `zellij action dump-screen`
+   for the prompt text, (c) sends Enter only once the prompt is rendered,
+   and (d) detaches the transient client. Bounded by a 30 s timeout.
+
+This is a **skill + scripts change**: `skills/launch/SKILL.md` plus one
+new shell helper. No TypeScript, no daemon change, no `bindings.json`
+schema change, no MCP protocol change, no zellij config file. The
+existing PreToolUse hook on `AskUserQuestion` (in `hooks/hooks.json`) and
+the existing `discord_ask` MCP tool are untouched.
+
+## Trust gate
+
+The skill identifies "Discord-triggered" the same way the existing trust
+model already does (`skills/launch/SKILL.md` §Trust model): the
+**immediately preceding context contains a `<channel source="discord"
+...>` notification that drove this invocation**. When that is the case,
+the new `discord_ask` gates fire. When it is not (i.e. the user typed
+`/discord:launch ...` in their terminal), no gate fires and behavior is
+identical to today.
+
+This matches the existing pattern used by `purge`'s terminal-only refusal:
+trust-path detection is already specified, this change just adds two new
+"if Discord-triggered, ask first" sites on top of it.
+
+## SKILL.md changes
+
+### `start` — add launch gate (new step 1A)
+
+Insert between step 1 (cwd validation) and step 2 (git detection):
+
+> 1A. **(Discord-triggered only) Confirm launch via `discord_ask`.** If
+> this invocation was driven by a `<channel source="discord" ...>`
+> message, post
+> `discord_ask("确认在 <abs> 启动一个新的 Claude 会话?", options=[确认启动, 取消])`.
+> - No / timeout → abort. Nothing was created yet, so no cleanup needed.
+> - Yes → continue.
+
+### `start` — robust dev-channels Enter (rewrite step 8)
+
+Step 8 becomes:
+
+```sh
+# Wait for the dev-channels prompt and send Enter only when it is rendered.
+# Helper internally attaches a transient pty client (zellij action only
+# delivers to sessions with at least one attached client). 30 s timeout;
+# on failure tell the user to attach manually.
+if ! /workspaces/claude-discord-multisession/scripts/await-dev-channels-prompt.sh "$session"; then
+  echo "dev-channels prompt did not appear within 30s — attach to '$session' and press Enter manually"
+fi
+```
+
+Step 7 (the zellij session creation) is unchanged — no `--config` is
+added; the default pane created by `attach --create-background` is
+replaced by the Claude pane in the existing `run --in-place
+--close-replaced-pane` invocation, so no startup-tip overlay is present
+on the active pane when the helper runs.
+
+### `start` — verify step 3 binding-conflict ask actually fires
+
+Step 3 already specifies `discord_ask`. The change here is documentation
+hygiene: explicitly note that the same trust-gate (`<channel source=
+"discord" ...>` in context) decides terminal vs. discord, and require
+the integration test in §Testing to cover it.
+
+### `stop` — add confirmation gate (new step 0)
+
+Insert before step 1 (resolve target → sid):
+
+> 0. **(Discord-triggered only) Confirm via `discord_ask`.** If this
+> invocation was driven by a `<channel source="discord" ...>` message,
+> post `discord_ask("确认 stop <target>?", options=[确认 stop, 取消])`.
+> No / timeout → abort.
+
+`purge` is unchanged — it is already terminal-only.
+
+### `allowed-tools` frontmatter
+
+Add one entry:
+
+```
+Bash(/workspaces/claude-discord-multisession/scripts/await-dev-channels-prompt.sh *)
+```
+
+## `scripts/await-dev-channels-prompt.sh`
+
+New shell helper, sibling of `derive-binding-key.sh`.
+
+**Interface**
+
+```
+await-dev-channels-prompt.sh <session_name> [timeout_seconds]
+```
+
+- `session_name` — zellij session to inspect (required).
+- `timeout_seconds` — default `30`.
+- Exit `0` once Enter has been sent.
+- Exit non-zero on timeout. Diagnostic goes to stderr; stdout stays clean.
+
+**Algorithm**
+
+```
+sentinel = "I am using this for local development"
+tmp = client_pid_file = client_pgid = ""   # init empty before the trap
+
+# Register cleanup BEFORE creating temp files, so a failing mktemp still
+# reaps whatever exists. rm -f tolerates the empty initial values.
+cleanup() {
+  rm -f "$tmp" "$client_pid_file"
+  [ -n "$client_pgid" ] && kill -TERM -"$client_pgid"   # reap transient client
+}
+trap cleanup EXIT
+tmp=$(mktemp); client_pid_file=$(mktemp)
+
+# Attach a transient pty-backed client so `zellij action` has a client to
+# deliver to. script(1) provides the pty — but script(1) reassigns its
+# child to a FRESH process group, so $! (the script pid) cannot reap the
+# inner `zellij attach`. So wrap the zellij call in `bash -c` that records
+# its own PID — which equals that inner process group's id — into
+# client_pid_file before exec'ing zellij. SHELL=/bin/bash forces
+# script(1)'s `$SHELL -c` to expand $$ in bash.
+SHELL=/bin/bash setsid script -qfc \
+  "bash -c 'echo \$\$ > $client_pid_file; exec env -u ZELLIJ -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME zellij attach $session'" \
+  /dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+
+# Poll up to ~2 s for the wrapper to record the inner PID.
+for up to 20 tries: if client_pid_file non-empty: client_pgid=$(cat it); break; else sleep 0.1
+if client_pgid still empty: warn to stderr (transient client may not be reaped)
+
+# Poll for the prompt.
+deadline = now + timeout
+while now < deadline:
+  env -u ZELLIJ -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME \
+    zellij -s "$session" action dump-screen --path "$tmp"
+  if grep -q "$sentinel" "$tmp"; then
+    env -u ZELLIJ -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME \
+      zellij -s "$session" action send-keys "Enter"
+    exit 0   # trap runs: removes temp files, reaps transient client
+  fi
+  sleep 0.5
+
+print "'<sentinel>' not seen in <timeout>s" to stderr
+exit 1       # trap runs: removes temp files, reaps transient client
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- The transient client lives only for the duration of the helper (worst
+  case: 30 s). The launch flow does not need a client otherwise — the
+  Claude process inside the session runs regardless of whether anyone is
+  attached.
+- `zellij action` is a silent no-op against a session with no client, so
+  the transient client is mandatory. Because `script(1)` reassigns its
+  child to a fresh process group, the helper records the inner process's
+  PID (via the `bash -c 'echo $$'` wrapper) — that PID is the
+  process-group id, and `kill -TERM -$client_pgid` reaps the `zellij
+  attach` and its descendants. If the PID is never recorded within ~2 s
+  the helper warns on stderr.
+- `dump-screen --path` writes the focused pane viewport; once the transient
+  client is attached the focused pane is the Claude pane created by
+  `zellij run --in-place --close-replaced-pane`, so the prompt lands
+  there.
+- `send-keys "Enter"` is the documented key-name form (the side experiment
+  confirmed `write-chars` is for text and `send-keys` is for key names).
+- All `zellij` calls are prefixed `env -u ZELLIJ -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME`
+  to match the rest of the skill — the helper never targets the caller's
+  zellij session.
+- The script is idempotent: once Enter is sent and exit 0 is returned, it
+  is not re-invoked by the skill.
+
+## Data flow
+
+Discord-triggered `start` (the changed path):
+
+```
+Discord message → host Claude
+  └─ /discord:launch start <cwd>
+     ├─ 1.  cwd validation (unchanged)
+     ├─ 1A. discord_ask("启动 <cwd>?")  ─── NEW
+     │      └─ no/timeout → abort, nothing created
+     ├─ 2.  git detection (unchanged)
+     ├─ 3.  binding-conflict discord_ask (already in SKILL.md, now
+     │      explicitly trust-gated and test-covered)
+     ├─ 4.  git worktree add (unchanged)
+     ├─ 5.  derive sid (unchanged)
+     ├─ 6.  check existing zellij session (unchanged)
+     ├─ 7.  zellij attach --create-background (unchanged)
+     ├─ 8a. zellij run … claude --dangerously-load-… (unchanged)
+     ├─ 8b. await-dev-channels-prompt.sh <session>  ─── REPLACES sleep+write 13
+     │       (helper internally: attach transient pty client →
+     │        poll dump-screen → send Enter → detach client)
+     │      └─ timeout → warn user, leave session running for manual Enter
+     └─ 9.  poll bindings.json for thread_id (unchanged)
+```
+
+Discord-triggered `stop`:
+
+```
+Discord message → host Claude
+  └─ /discord:launch stop <target>
+     ├─ 0. discord_ask("stop <target>?")  ─── NEW
+     │     └─ no/timeout → abort
+     ├─ 1. resolve sid (unchanged)
+     ├─ 2. zellij kill-session (unchanged)
+     └─ 3. report (unchanged)
+```
+
+Terminal-triggered paths: identical to today, except step 8 uses the new
+helper instead of `sleep 3 && action write 13`. The helper produces no
+output on success, so the terminal user sees the same launch summary as
+before.
+
+## Error handling
+
+| Failure | Symptom | Behavior |
+|---|---|---|
+| `discord_ask` timeout (10 min default) | user did not click | treat as cancel: abort; if a worktree was already created in step 4, leave it on disk and report the path so the user can remove it later |
+| `await-dev-channels-prompt.sh` timeout (30 s) | prompt never seen | non-zero exit; skill prints "attach to `<session>` and press Enter manually"; do not kill the session |
+| Transient pty client fails to attach (`script` missing, attach refused) | `dump-screen` returns empty repeatedly | helper keeps polling until deadline, then exits non-zero — user sees the same "attach and press Enter manually" guidance |
+| `dump-screen` itself fails | helper sees empty/missing dump | treat as not-yet-rendered, keep polling until deadline |
+| User runs another `stop` while `discord_ask` is pending | racing inputs | acceptable: whichever ask resolves first wins; the second one's kill is a no-op against an already-stopped session — step 2 already handles "no zellij session for sid" |
+| Helper killed mid-flight (Ctrl-C, parent exit) | transient client lingers | `trap … EXIT` reaps the transient client's process group on any exit path |
+
+The `purge` flow is unchanged. The PreToolUse hook on `AskUserQuestion`
+(`hooks/hooks.json`) is unchanged — it bridges model-level
+`AskUserQuestion` to Discord, which is orthogonal to the new explicit
+`discord_ask` calls inside the SKILL.md instructions.
+
+## Testing strategy
+
+1. **Unit test for the helper.** `tests/await-dev-channels-prompt.test.ts`
+   (or `.sh`). Boot a real zellij background session, `zellij run` a
+   fixture command that prints the prompt sentinel string and then
+   `read`s a line (writing it to a marker file on receipt). Run the
+   helper. Assert (a) helper exits 0, (b) the marker file contains the
+   line the fixture was supposed to receive — proving Enter was actually
+   delivered to the pane. Two additional cases: a timeout case (fixture
+   that never prints the sentinel → helper exits non-zero within 30 s),
+   and a cleanup case (helper killed mid-poll → no leftover `script` or
+   `zellij attach` processes from its transient client).
+2. **Integration coverage for the `discord_ask` gates.** Extend
+   `tests/daemon-shim.integration.test.ts` with:
+   - Discord-triggered `start` where the mocked `discord_ask` returns
+     **cancel** → assert no zellij session is created and no
+     `bindings.json` entry is added.
+   - Discord-triggered `start` where `discord_ask` returns **confirm** →
+     assert the existing happy-path expectations still pass.
+   - Discord-triggered `stop` cancel/confirm → analogous.
+   - Discord-triggered `start` against a repo with an existing in-place
+     binding → assert the step-3 `discord_ask` fires and the chosen branch
+     is taken.
+3. **Terminal-triggered regression.** Existing tests that drive `start`
+   and `stop` from a terminal trust path must continue to pass with no
+   modification — verifying the gates are dormant outside the Discord
+   trust path.
+4. **Manual smoke.** From Discord: `/discord:launch start
+   /workspaces/<repo>` → see the launch ask, confirm, see the session and
+   thread come up cleanly with no terminal warnings about the
+   dev-channels prompt. From Discord: `/discord:launch stop <sid>` →
+   see the stop ask, confirm, session goes away. From terminal: same two
+   commands, no ask appears.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Eliminating the `--dangerously-load-development-channels` flag itself
+  (would require upstream work to add a no-prompt env var or a
+  pre-acceptance file — that is the "approach C" we rejected).
+- Shipping a zellij config file. The startup-tip overlay was originally
+  on the table as a separate failure mode, but the launch flow's
+  `run --in-place --close-replaced-pane` already replaces the default
+  pane (and the tip with it) before the helper runs, so no config is
+  needed.
+- Adding `discord_ask` confirmations to `purge` (already terminal-only).
+- Changing the `AskUserQuestion` PreToolUse hook or the discord MCP
+  server. Those are working; this design only adds explicit
+  `discord_ask` calls inside skill instructions.
+- Touching `bindings.json` schema, daemon, or shim — none of those are
+  affected.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The side experiment that motivated this design (testing whether
+  programmatically `attach + send-keys` can deliver to a zellij session)
+  confirmed the approach is viable but only under two conditions
+  **relevant to the launch flow**: an attached client, and `send-keys`
+  used with key names rather than text. (A third condition — startup
+  tips dismissed — is a real issue in a naive `zellij attach -c` shell,
+  but does not apply here because `run --in-place --close-replaced-pane`
+  replaces the default pane.) The helper satisfies both relevant
+  conditions: it attaches a transient pty client for the duration of the
+  Enter delivery, and it uses `send-keys "Enter"` rather than text.
+- This change composes cleanly with the existing zellij and worktree
+  designs (`2026-05-21-zellij-launch-design.md`,
+  `2026-05-21-worktree-launch-design.md`): worktree mode picks the cwd,
+  zellij is the backend, and this refactor only touches the confirmation
+  surface on top of both.
