+# tmux → zellij launch backend — design
+
+Date: 2026-05-21
+Topic: `/discord:launch` spawns zellij sessions instead of tmux sessions
+
+## Problem
+
+The `/discord:launch` skill spawns detached **tmux** sessions. The user
+manages their devcontainer/pod with **zellij**. tmux and zellij are separate
+multiplexers with separate namespaces — a tmux session never appears in
+`zellij list-sessions`, so the user cannot see, attach, or manage launched
+Claude sessions from their normal zellij workflow.
+
+## Solution overview
+
+Replace tmux with zellij throughout `skills/launch/SKILL.md`. Each
+`/discord:launch start` creates one independent **background (detached)
+zellij session** per launched Claude. tmux is dropped entirely (no
+configurable toggle).
+
+This is a **skill-only change**: only `skills/launch/SKILL.md` is edited. No
+TypeScript, no daemon change, no `bindings.json` schema change. The binding
+key (`sid`) and the daemon are untouched.
+
+This change composes with the worktree-launch feature (see
+`2026-05-21-worktree-launch-design.md`): worktree mode decides the cwd; the
+zellij backend is what launches Claude in that cwd. They are orthogonal.
+
+## Session naming
+
+The tmux backend named sessions `claude-<sid>`. The zellij backend names
+them:
+
+```
+claude-<basename>-<sid>
+```
+
+- `<sid>` — the 12-hex binding key from `derive-binding-key.sh`, unchanged.
+- `<basename>` — the launch cwd's basename, sanitized: every character
+  outside `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` is replaced with `-`.
+- The `bindings.json` key remains the bare `<sid>` — unchanged. Only the
+  multiplexer session name gains the basename, for human readability in
+  `zellij list-sessions` and `zellij attach`.
+
+**sid extraction from a session name:** `sid="${name##*-}"` — the substring
+after the final `-`. The `<sid>` is always the trailing 12-hex segment, so
+this is correct even when `<basename>` itself contains `-` (e.g.
+`connectors-operator`). The skill validates the result against
+`^[0-9a-f]{12}$`.
+
+**Worktree composition:** worktree mode produces cwd
+`/workspaces/.worktrees/<repo>-<label>`, so its basename is `<repo>-<label>`
+and the session name becomes `claude-<repo>-<label>-<sid>` — the repo and
+the worktree label are both visible in the name.
+
+Examples:
+
+| launch | cwd | zellij session name |
+|---|---|---|
+| in-place `/workspaces/connectors-operator` | `/workspaces/connectors-operator` | `claude-connectors-operator-2803b9995692` |
+| worktree of `connectors-operator`, label `feat-x` | `/workspaces/.worktrees/connectors-operator-feat-x` | `claude-connectors-operator-feat-x-<sid>` |
+
+## Command mapping
+
+Every `zellij` invocation in the skill runs with `ZELLIJ` and
+`ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME` unset so the skill never accidentally targets the
+caller's own zellij session:
+
+```sh
+env -u ZELLIJ -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME zellij ...
+```
+
+| Purpose | tmux (old) | zellij (new) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Create detached session | `tmux new-session -d -s claude-<sid> -c DIR 'CMD'` | `zellij attach --create-background <name>` |
+| Run Claude in it | (part of `new-session`) | `zellij -s <name> run --in-place --close-replaced-pane --close-on-exit --cwd DIR -- bash -lc 'CMD'` |
+| Confirm dev-channels prompt | `tmux send-keys -t <name> Enter` | `zellij -s <name> action write 13` |
+| Check a session exists | `tmux has-session -t claude-<sid>` | `zellij list-sessions --no-formatting`, find a name ending `-<sid>` |
+| List sessions | `tmux ls -F ...` | `zellij list-sessions` |
+| Kill session (`stop`) | `tmux kill-session -t claude-<sid>` | `zellij kill-session <name>` |
+| Full delete (`purge`) | (tmux had no separate step) | `zellij delete-session <name> --force` |
+
+`<name>` is the full `claude-<basename>-<sid>` session name.
+
+### Why `run --in-place --close-replaced-pane`
+
+`zellij attach --create-background` creates the session with one default
+shell pane. `run --in-place --close-replaced-pane` replaces that default
+pane with the Claude pane and closes the shell pane, leaving a clean
+single-pane session — equivalent to what `tmux new-session -d ... 'CMD'`
+produced.
+
+Implementation note: verify `--in-place --close-replaced-pane` behaves
+correctly against a freshly created background session during
+implementation. If it does not, the fallback is to `run` Claude as a new
+pane and leave (or separately close) the default shell pane — the default
+shell pane is harmless, just untidy.
+
+### dev-channels confirmation
+
+`claude --dangerously-load-development-channels ...` shows an interactive
+"I am using this for local development" prompt on every launch. The tmux
+backend handled this ad hoc (a manual Enter keystroke); the zellij backend
+makes it an explicit step: after launching, wait ~3 seconds for the prompt,
+then `zellij -s <name> action write 13` (byte 13 = carriage return) to
+confirm. After `run`, the Claude pane is the focused pane, so the keystroke
+lands in it.
+
+## Per-verb changes in `skills/launch/SKILL.md`
+
+### `start`
+
+The `start` section's multiplexer-agnostic steps are unchanged: cwd
+validation, git detection / worktree creation (worktree spec), sid
+derivation, thread_id polling. The changes:
+
+- Compute the session name `name="claude-<sanitized-basename>-<sid>"`.
+- **Existing-session check:** `zellij list-sessions --no-formatting`; look
+  for a session whose name ends `-<sid>`.
+  - If a **running** session exists → do not relaunch; report it and stop.
+  - If an **exited** session exists (zellij keeps killed sessions as
+    resurrectable) → `zellij delete-session <name> --force`, then continue
+    so a fresh session is created (never resurrect a stale one).
+- **Launch:** `zellij attach --create-background <name>`, then
+  `zellij -s <name> run --in-place --close-replaced-pane --close-on-exit
+  --cwd <launch_cwd> -- bash -lc '<CMD>'`. `<CMD>` is
+  `DISCORD_THREAD_ID=auto [DISCORD_THREAD_NAME=<label>] claude
+  --dangerously-load-development-channels plugin:discord@danielfbm-discord`.
+- **Confirm prompt:** wait ~3 s, then `zellij -s <name> action write 13`.
+- Report: sid, launch cwd, **zellij session name**, thread_id (and, in
+  worktree mode, the source repo + branch).
+
+### `list`
+
+`zellij list-sessions` instead of `tmux ls`. For each session whose name
+starts with `claude-`: extract `sid="${name##*-}"`, look up `cwd` and
+`thread_id` in `bindings.json`, derive `branch` via
+`git -C "$cwd" branch --show-current`. Render a markdown table with columns:
+
+```
+session | cwd | branch | thread_id | created
+```
+
+`session` is the full zellij name (what the user passes to `zellij attach`).
+`created` uses zellij's own "Created … ago" text (zellij `list-sessions`
+does not expose a raw epoch). If `zellij list-sessions` exits non-zero or no
+`claude-*` session exists, print "no sessions running".
+
+### `stop`
+
+Resolve the target to a `sid` exactly as today. Then find the full session
+name: `zellij list-sessions --no-formatting`, the name ending `-<sid>`. Then
+`zellij kill-session <name>`. `bindings.json` is left untouched (binding
+preserved for reattach) — unchanged in spirit. The cwd / worktree are
+untouched — unchanged.
+
+### `purge` (terminal-only)
+
+The terminal-only refusal rule is unchanged. The session-killing steps
+become: find the session name for the sid, `zellij kill-session <name>`,
+then `zellij delete-session <name> --force` (zellij keeps killed sessions as
+resurrectable; the explicit delete prevents a later `start` from finding a
+stale resurrectable session). Then delete the `bindings.json` entry and run
+the worktree-cleanup step — both unchanged from the worktree spec.
+
+### `allowed-tools` frontmatter
+
+Replace `Bash(tmux *)` with `Bash(zellij *)`. Add `Bash(env *)` (for the
+`env -u … zellij` wrapper). Add `Bash(sleep *)` if not already permitted
+(needed for the dev-channels confirmation wait).
+
+### Implementation notes section
+
+Update tmux-specific notes to zellij. In particular, the note that
+`tmux new-session -d` starts a server on demand becomes the zellij
+equivalent, and the one-sid-per-session invariant is now enforced by
+zellij session names rather than `tmux has-session`.
+
+## Pre-existing tmux sessions
+
+Claude sessions launched before this change run in tmux (e.g. the current
+`claude-3c14130d2916` management session and `claude-2803b9995692`
+connectors-operator). After this change the skill has no tmux commands, so
+it can no longer `list`/`stop`/`purge` those sessions.
+
+There is no automatic migration. Pre-existing tmux sessions must be managed
+directly with `tmux` (`tmux ls`, `tmux kill-session`) until they are
+stopped. Once stopped and re-launched via `/discord:launch start`, they come
+back as zellij sessions. This is a one-time transition cost and is
+documented in the skill's Implementation notes.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- No configurable tmux/zellij toggle — zellij fully replaces tmux.
+- No retroactive migration of running tmux sessions.
+- No "N tabs in one shared zellij session" model — each launched Claude is
+  its own independent zellij session.
+- No change to sid hashing, `bindings.json` schema, or the daemon.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `skills/launch/SKILL.md` — frontmatter `allowed-tools`; the `start`,
+  `list`, `stop`, `purge`, and Implementation-notes sections.
